# Kept out of the image's build context, so a local build sees what CI's clean checkout does.
# `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile would otherwise lay the host's node_modules over the container's own,
# Windows-native binaries included, and Vite would bake a local .env file into the bundle.
# Never `.*`: the Dockerfile copies .npmrc, whose engine-strict guards the image's install (ADR-030).
node_modules
dist
coverage
.vite
.env*
